name>Klepp</surname><given-names>K-I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Validity and reproducibility of self-reported intake of fruit and vegetable among 6th graders</article-title><source>Eur J Clin Nutr</source><year>2004</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>771</fpage><lpage>777</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15116080</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.ejcn.1601875</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pinheiro</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bates</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><source>Mixed-Effects models in S and S-Plus</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>New York: Springer</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wells</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The National School Fruit Scheme produces short-term but not longer-term increases in fruit consumption in primary school children</article-title><source>Br J Nutr</source><year>2005</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>537</fpage><lpage>542</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15946417</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1079/BJN20051393</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bere</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Veier&#x000f8;d</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><name><surname>Bjelland</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Klepp</surname><given-names>K-I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Outcome and process evaluation of a Norwegian school-randomized fruit and vegetable intervention: Fruits and Vegetables Make the Marks (FVMM)</article-title><source>Health Educ Res</source><year>2006</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>258</fpage><lpage>267</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16219631</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/her/cyh062</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>